    "section": "7.19",
    "heading": "Verbal (V)",
    "lineStart": 7277,
    "lineEnd": 7279
  },
  "section": "7.19",
  "rulesText": "A Verbal component is the chanting of esoteric words that sound like nonsense to the uninitiated. The words must be uttered in a normal speaking voice. The words themselves aren't the source of the spell's power; rather, the particular combination of sounds, with specific pitch and resonance, sets the threads of magic in motion. Thus, a creature who is gagged or in an area of magical silence can't cast a spell with a Verbal component."
}
